WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.971
Measuring intraocular pressure in clinic.

2
00:00:03.421 --> 00:00:08.355
Applanation technique, common sources of error and how corneal thickness changes the reading.

3
00:00:08.805 --> 00:00:15.911
A full assessment combines pressure measurement, gonioscopy, optic disc examination and visual field testing.

4
00:00:16.361 --> 00:00:20.494
Optical coherence tomography helps document the nerve fibre layer over time.

5
00:00:20.944 --> 00:00:24.438
Lowering pressure is the only proven way to slow progression.

6
00:00:24.888 --> 00:00:29.637
A target pressure is set for each patient and reviewed if the disease continues to progress.

7
00:00:30.087 --> 00:00:33.129
Up to half of patients do not use drops as prescribed.

8
00:00:33.579 --> 00:00:38.757
Simple regimens, instillation training and regular review of technique improve outcomes.
